<title>INDONESIA: Indonesian central bank raises band by one point.</title>
<headline>Indonesian central bank raises band by one point.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's central bank, Bank Indonesia, raised its daily fixing of the dollar-rupiah intervention band by one point to 2,378/2,682 on Monday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The band sets the parameters for central bank intervention in the foreign exchange market.</p>
<p>Dealers said the band fixing had become a subject of market attention after the rupiah plunged on speculative attacks in morning trading, sending the currency to a historic low of 2,650/55.</p>
<p>Spot rupiah was quoted at 2,620/30 at 0815 GMT.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
